"efficient_model_loading" = "By default, we unload the model after image generation and load the model back when generating again. The model loading process can take anywhere between 2 to 5 seconds each time. If enabled, we will keep the model in memory for faster generation and only unload it when the operating system notifies us that we are running low on memory. Optionally, you can choose to only preload the CoreML model, which can reduce the CoreML model loading time and doesn't use additional memory.";

"coreml_if_possible" = "Use CoreML for SD 1.5 If Possible";

"coreml_memory_usage" = "CoreML consumes more memory and may not be suitable for many mobile devices. It takes approximately 70 seconds to load for the first time. However, in return, it is about 50% faster. It is best to enable 'Keep Model in Memory - Preload' alongside it to reuse the first time load.";

"coreml_for_lora" = "Use CoreML w/ LoRA for SD 1.5";

"coreml_lora_detail" = "For LoRA models, CoreML can be leveraged. However, each change in weights, different LoRA models, or their combinations will generate a new CoreML model, incurring model compilation which can take several minutes.";

"file_swap_weights" = "File-Swap Weights";

"file_swap_detail" = "The core operation of Stable Diffusion requires at least 1.7GiB for parameters. Mobile devices with 3GiB of RAM might struggle to load these parameters. This option allows us to offload these parameters to disk and load them only on-demand. For slower devices, this will not be a bottleneck, but for faster devices, it could be. Additional disk space is required for this, and choosing 'Never' will force us to remove these parameter files.";

"automatic_sometimes" = "Automatic (Sometimes)";

"screen_saver" = "Screen Saver";

"screen_saver_detail" = "On mobile devices, the app must be in the foreground to continue image generation. Excessive use of the phone at a high screen brightness might cause a lasting effect on the OLED screen (typically seen on iPhone Pro models). The screen saver will reduce the screen brightness during image generation to avoid potential negative effects.";

"temporary_directory" = "Temporary Directory";

"temporary_directory_detail" = "Due to how the OS works internally, 'Local Code' might generate excessive temporary files under a temporary directory. These files will be automatically removed when the OS is running low on disk space. However, you can also use this option to clean it up explicitly if you are running low on disk space.";

"cleanup" = "Cleanup";

"reset_to_default" = "Reset to Default";

"seed_explain" = "Seed value determines how image generation starts. The same seed will generate the same image.";

"seed_explain_cli" = "Seed value determines how image generation starts. The same seed will generate the same image. Note that passing -1 for the seed will cause it generate a random value.";

"seed_mode" = "Seed Mode";

"seed_mode_detail" = "Seed mode determines how the seed is used. \"Legacy\" is compatible with older Draw Things app, \"NVIDIA GPU Compatible\" is compatible with other desktop tools such as AUTOMATIC1111 or Invoke.AI on NVIDIA GPUs / Linux / Windows, \"Torch CPU Compatible\" is compatible with other desktop tools on macOS and \"Scale Alike\" allows the seed to maintain some resemblance even at different image sizes.";

"legacy" = "Legacy";

"image_size" = "Image Size";

"image_size_detail" = "The size of the generated image. For best results, use 1:1 / Normal";

"final_output_size" = "Final Output Size";

"upscaler_detail" = "Upscaler can help to generate a visually pleasant high-resolution image (e.g. 2048x2048) from a relatively smaller image (e.g. 512x512). Depending on the upscaler you use, it may fill in with different details and introduce subtly different styles.";

"steps_detail" = "How many steps are to be applied for image generation. Using more steps results in a better image, but will take longer.";

"text_guidance_detail" = "How \"literally\" the text input should be treated. A higher setting would be more faithful to the text, while a lower setting would allow more artistic liberty. (CFG Scale)";

"text_guidance_detail_cli" = "How \"literally\" the text input should be treated. Higher would be more faithful to the text while lower would have more artistic liberty. (CFG Scale). Note that the default gets changed to 0.7 if in image-to-image mode.";

"text_to_image" = "Text to Image";

"image_to_image" = "Image to Image";

"strength_detail" = "When generating from an image, a high value allows more artistic freedom from the original. 100% means no influence from the existing image (a.k.a. text to image).";

"dpm_2m_karras" = "DPM++ 2M Karras";

"sampler_detail" = "Different samplers can converge at different step counts and may result in different visual styles. Euler A is known to generate more \"dreamy\" images, while DPM++ 2M Karras can generate high-quality images in no more than 30 steps.";

"image_guidance_detail" = "Edit models use the image as guidance in the same way as the text. This value, in conjunction with text guidance, determines how the model can diverge from either. A higher image guidance would be more faithful to the original image.";

"clip_skip" = "CLIP Skip";

"clip_skip_detail" = "\"CLIP Skip\" controls how many layers from the last one in the text encoder are skipped. The text encoder translates your text into vectors that the computer understands. Skipping more layers in the text encoder will force the computer to focus more on individual words than their combined meanings. This might be useful for models that are fine-tuned on tag-like text inputs.";

"mask_blur" = "Mask Blur";

"mask_blur_detail" = "\"Mask Blur\" tries to make the mask a bit softer on the edge, which may help with blending with the rest of the image.";

"face_restoration_detail" = "Face restoration can use an additional model to fix the small, distorted faces during image generation. This process works best for photorealistic images. For anime or artistic images, this may not be desirable.";

"batch_size_detail" = "How many images to be generated simultaneously in a batch.";

"high_resolution_fix" = "High Resolution Fix";

"save_images_to" = "Save Generated Images to";

"save_images_detail" = "Generated images can be saved to a folder of your choice. This makes it easier if you use external applications to organize your generated images.";

