"orthonormal_lora_down" = "Fixed Orthonormal LoRA Down";

"orthonormal_lora_down_detail" = "LoRA training involves two sub-matrices: a down matrix that projects activation to small subspace, and a up matrix that projects back to the original output latents space. For LoRA, we are basically substitue y = (W + W')x to y = (W + BA)x where W' is the fine-tuning delta. We can fix the down matrix as a orthonormal matrix to force all fine-tuning happens on the B matrix. This helps us to get closer to the full fine-tuning dynamics by imposing stronger regularization constraint.";

