"causal_inference_every_n_frames" = "Every N Frames";

"causal_inference_detail" = "Causal inference takes into account only the current and preceding frames (not future ones), a method known as CausVid. This option is available only for video models specifically fine-tuned for causal generation. The “Every N Frames” setting controls the granularity of inference: instead of generating one frame at a time, the model generates frames in chunks of N, using all frames up to that point as context. For example, with N = 2, frames a and b are generated together using frames a–b as context; frames c and d are then generated using a–d as context, and so on.";

